  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Map HUD",
    "overview": "The minimap is the screen. On the route page it fills the first viewport, fitted so every camp stays visible and clickable, and sits on a blurred, darkened copy of itself. Everything else floats over it the way a game interface floats over the battlefield: a HUD bar across the top with the route name and actions, and a right column of panels for Hero and matchup, Hero level and the Route. Dark HUD panels are the default; a day scheme swaps them for white panels on a pale ground without changing the structure.\n\nThe system is quiet so the map can be loud. Panels are near-black plates with a 1px edge, an 8px corner and a soft shadow. Colour carries meaning, not decoration: route yellow marks what you press and where the hero goes, purple is experience, mana blue is waypoints and focus, green is the Ancient of War. Two type voices split the work: Chakra Petch, a squared technical face, for anything that reads as interface (titles, numbers, buttons, labels); Hanken Grotesk for anything a player reads. Density is high, numbers are tabular everywhere.\n\nOther pages (home, maps, builds, community) inherit the tokens, panels and controls but not the stage; the stage belongs to the route page.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Map-first: the minimap owns the first screen; panels float beside it and never cover camps.",
      "Dark by default, light as an equal second scheme with the same structure.",
      "One accent (route yellow) shared by the hero path, stop numbers and primary actions.",
      "Soft depth: blurred shadows, translucent panels, 1px edges, gently rounded corners.",
      "Stop states by shape: filled, dashed, ringed."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Yellow Rule",
        "body": "Route yellow means \"press this\" or \"the hero goes here\". It is the only fill on a primary button and the only colour of a stop number. Don't spend it on decoration, headings or panel chrome beyond the small title tab.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Map Keeps Its Colours Rule",
        "body": "Camp green, orange and red, hero yellow and AoW green come from the game and are not reinterpreted. Don't tint them toward the palette, and don't use the camp colours for site UI.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Dark Text On Yellow Rule",
        "body": "Text on yellow, blue or a game colour uses on-accent, which is dark in both schemes. Never use ink there; ink turns light at night.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Chakra Petch for interface and numbers, Hanken Grotesk for reading. Don't set a camp name or a note in Chakra Petch, and don't set a button in Hanken.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Numbers are tabular everywhere (set on body). XP columns must line up.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Map Is The Bottom Layer Rule",
        "body": "The map and its blurred copy are the lowest plane; everything interface floats above with the Float shadow. Nothing sits under the map.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** give the map the first screen on the route page and keep every camp visible; size the map to its container, never crop it.",
      "**Do** float interface on panel plates: panel fill, 1px edge, 8px corner, the Float shadow.",
      "**Do** mark a panel with its small colour tab (yellow to act, blue for reference) rather than a filled title bar.",
      "**Do** keep route yellow for primary actions, stop numbers and the hero path.",
      "**Do** use on-accent (dark) for text on yellow, blue and game colours in both schemes.",
      "**Do** show stop states by shape: filled, dashed, ringed.",
      "**Do** keep both schemes structurally identical; only the token values change."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use hard offset shadows or zero-blur shadows; depth here is soft.",
      "**Don't** add a second accent or use XP purple and mana blue for actions.",
      "**Don't** repaint the map: camp colours and path colours stay the game's.",
      "**Don't** set reading text in Chakra Petch or buttons in Hanken Grotesk.",
      "**Don't** put uppercase tracked labels above headings as section kickers; the uppercase field label is only for a caption directly above a control.",
      "**Don't** cover the map with panels on desktop; panels live in the right column."
    ]
  }
}